# CRM Milestone 18 — this file did not exist before this milestone. Its
# absence was a real deployment risk: NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are inlined
# into the JavaScript bundle at BUILD time (not read at runtime), so a
# `next build` run without this variable explicitly set in the build
# environment silently bakes in whatever .env.local happens to contain —
# which, in this repo, is http://localhost:3001 (see .env.local). A
# production build must have this set in the hosting platform's own build
# environment variables; there is no in-app fallback that could catch a
# missing/wrong value after the fact.

# Base URL of the IVYHUTS backend (the ivyhuts-website repo's api/* Vercel
# functions) — the ONLY backend this CRM talks to. See
# src/lib/api/client.ts: every request goes through this one base URL, with
# the session cookie sent via credentials:"include". The CRM never talks to
# MongoDB/Redis directly.
#
# Local dev value (matches scripts/local-api-server.js's default
# LOCAL_API_PORT in the ivyhuts-website repo):
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Production value: NOT filled in here — as of this milestone, the
# ivyhuts-website backend has no deployed production URL yet (no custom
# domain configured in its vercel.json). Do not guess one. Once that
# backend is deployed, set this to its real HTTPS URL in the CRM's own
# Vercel project environment variables (Production scope), and set the
# backend's CRM_ORIGIN to this CRM's own deployed URL in return — the two
# are a matched pair (see ivyhuts-website/.env.example's CRM_ORIGIN
# comment). A build without this set correctly will silently ship pointing
# at localhost, which fails closed (every request errors) rather than
# leaking data — but still breaks the app, so treat this as a hard
# pre-deploy checklist item, not something to discover after the fact.
